<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Fanakati</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1282</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Fanakati was a Central Asian Muslim from Banakat who served as chief finance minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> for some twenty years. He raised revenue through monopolies and higher taxes and placed his relatives in office, which made him widely hated among Chinese officials. He was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a> in 1282, after which Kublai condemned him posthumously.</p></div>
